699245695, "item_size": 2393511607, "metadata": {"mediatype": "movies", "collection": ["Comedy_Films", "feature_films", "moviesandfilms"], "title": "My Man Godfrey (1936)", "description": "A ditzy socialite finds a homeless man for a scavenger hunt and then hires him as their butler.", "subject": "William Powell; Carole Lombard; Alice Brady; Gail Patrick; Eugene Pallette; Jean Dixon; Alan Mowbray; Mischa Auer; Pat Flaherty; Robert Light; Mystic Nights Videos", "runtime": "1:34:47", "sound": "sound", "licenseurl": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/publicdomain/", "identifier": "MyManGodfrey1936", "uploader": "ephill@comcast.net", "addeddate": "2010-09-07 11:03:49", "publicdate": "2010-09-07 13:01:26", "backup_location": "ia903606_11", "ia_orig__runtime": "94 minutes 47 seconds"}, "reviews": [{"reviewbody": "But do we really need a third version of it on the Archive?\n\nPrevious uploads:\n\nhttp://www.archive.org/details/my_man_godfrey\n\nor\n\nhttp://www.archive.org/details/MyManGodfrey", "reviewtitle": "THIS ONE IS A 5 STAR WINNER!", "reviewer": "kareneliot", "reviewdate": "2010-09-09 15:08:42", "createdate": "2010-09-09 15:08:42", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "Yes, We do need a third version, The other two are chopped up and poor quality. This is the best version uploaded so far and I thank the person for uploading it. \n\nPeople should not be discouraged from uploading a movie Just because another version is available. Maybe you should spend more time uploading and less time moaning because someone uploaded the same movie,", "reviewtitle": "@kareneliot", "reviewer": "danielps2fan", "reviewdate": "2010-09-15 16:24:59", "createdate": "2010-09-15 16:24:59", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "Absolutely great film. Godfrey Smith sticking it to the upper crust, yet ultimately validating the American dream of ethical capitalism in a way that could even best old George Bailey. If only Godfrey...", "reviewtitle": "American liberal capitalism at its best", "reviewer": "Modern Art Otriad", "reviewdate": "2010-11-19 22:23:37", "createdate": "2010-11-19 22:23:37", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "Excellent film. Nominated for six Academy Awards, this is a classic among classics!", "reviewtitle": "Fantastic!", "reviewer": "Hemmingway", "reviewdate": "2012-01-24 04:26:12", "createdate": "2012-01-24 04:26:12", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "just watch,. it'll get you too,.", "reviewtitle": "one of my top films of all time,. love this!", "reviewer": "Futuristfood", "reviewdate": "2013-06-24 06:57:35", "createdate": "2013-06-24 06:57:35", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "William Powell, while quite an excellent and capable actor, could not convince me he was a butler. This is truly a great movie and perfect for the late, late show, which is where I saw it for the first time!", "reviewtitle": "William Powell", "reviewer": "disco07", "reviewdate": "2013-09-03 02:19:45", "createdate": "2013-09-03 02:19:45", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "The \"forgotten men\" in this movie are what we now call \"homeless\" people.  Thousands of those \"forgottten men\" were WWI vets that came home from the war to find that after they had served their country, there was really no longer a place for them at home.  They had many of the same mental and physical challenges that our service men and women today suffer.\nI absolutely LOVE William Powell.  He is great as Godfrey.\nThis movie is great to find here for free.  This one along with \"Arsenic and Old Lace\", \"The Awful Truth\" and \"Libeled Lady\" are some of the best of the \"screwball comedies\".", "reviewtitle": "This one is very good.", "reviewer": "I_h8_screen_names", "reviewdate": "2013-10-29 00:18:08", "createdate": "2013-10-29 00:18:08", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewbody": "I love my man Godfrey I watch it quite often and each cast member has done their job wonderfully  \nWilliam Powell is amazing as Godfrey and Carole Lombard as Irene and a special mention to Alice Brady as Angelica she is so funny! \n", "reviewtitle": "Justine Dean", "reviewer": "Justine Dean", "reviewer_itemname": "@justine_dean", "reviewdate": "2019-10-07 16:47:42", "createdate": "2019-10-07 16:47:42", "stars": "5"}, {"reviewtitle": "Continuity Error", "reviewbody": "Not reviewing the movie (Love it!), but there is a duplicate scene from about 1:00:07 to about 1:00:35.\n", "stars": "5", "reviewer": "The Most Famous Blurt", "reviewdate": "2021-08-07 03:03:43", "createdate": "2021-08-07 03:03:43", "reviewer_itemname": "@the_most_famous_blurt"}, {"reviewtitle": "Excellent movie", "reviewbody": "It was very entertaining.  I think another reviewer mentioned a duplicated interval in the movie around 1 hour in.  I noticed that too.  The duplicated part was just a couple minutes so it didn't hurt the viewing experience much.", "stars": "4", "reviewer": "IARRCSim", "reviewdate": "2023-11-06 04:41:26", "createdate": "2023-11-06 04:41:26", "reviewer_itemname": "@iarrcsim"}], "server": "dn600307.us.archive.org", "simplelists": {"solo_manifest": {"solo_manifest_dn600307": {"sys_changed_by": {"source": "task", "task_id": "5430926529"}, "sys_last_changed": "2026-06-11 15:08:20.923356"}}}, "solo": true, "uniq": 139394395, "workable_servers": ["dn600307.us.archive.org"]}